# ADR-002 — Permission Model (AI Enforcement Version)

## Core Rule

ALL permissions (read and write) are business rules and MUST live in the Domain layer.

There are no free reads.

## Authoritative Permission Source

	•	Permissions MUST be implemented as semantic methods on Domain entities
	•	Role comparisons (user.role === …) are FORBIDDEN outside Domain
	•	UI, hooks, and repositories MUST NOT decide permissions

## Correct

```ts
user.canRequestVacation()
user.canApproveVacation(vacation)
user.canViewVacation(vacation)
user.canApproveUserRegistration()
```

Forbidden

```ts
if (user.role === 'ADMIN') { ... }        // ❌
if (isManager || isAdmin) { ... }         // ❌
if (!permissionsFromUI) { ... }           // ❌
```


## Application Layer Rules

-	Use Cases MUST call Domain permission methods
-	Unauthorized actions MUST return Result.fail(UnauthorizedError)
-	Read Use Cases MUST:
-	filter results using Domain permission methods
-	or explicitly deny access

## Presentation Layer Rules

-	UI and hooks:
-	MUST NOT check roles
-	MUST NOT infer permissions
-	MUST NOT filter data for security
-	UI receives:
-	already-authorized data
-	permission flags as DTOs

## Permission Matrix (Hard Contract)

Vacation Requests

| Action          | COLLABORATOR | MANAGER | ADMIN |
|----------       |--------|---------|-------|
| Request Vacation | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Approve / Reject | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |-  
| View Own | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| View Team | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ |
| View all | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |

User Registration

| Action          | COLLABORATOR | MANAGER | ADMIN |
|----------       |--------|---------|-------|
| Register User   | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Approve Registration | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |
| View Pending Registrations | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |


⸻

Enforcement Rules (AI)

If you need a permission check and it does not exist:
	1.	STOP
	2.	Add a semantic method to the Domain entity
	3.	Enforce it in the Use Case
	4.	Expose the result as data to the UI

ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN
	•	Permission logic in UI or hooks
	•	Treating read operations as unprotected
	•	Role checks outside Domain
	•	Security filtering in Presentation
	•	“Quick fixes” to make tests pass

